* Mon Oct 19 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First package. Runs swtpm as a TPM 2.0 on a unix socket under systemd, as
  waydroid-swtpm.service, for the host-side keystore backend of docs/65 on a
  host with no usable hardware TPM. Stage 0 of that plan: nothing inside Android
  can see it yet, and it buys no security property over the image's software
  keymaster -- its state is a file on the same disk.
- Ships waydroid-tpm-check, the same TPM 2.0 sequence through any TCTI: this
  socket by default, /dev/tpmrm0 with --tcti. Transient objects only, no NV
  writes, never clears.
- The check flushes what it loads, because it has to: swtpm has no resource
  manager and tpm2-tools leave every object they load behind, so the third
  object fails TPM_RC_OBJECT_MEMORY and swtpm refuses everything until it
  restarts. docs/65's own swtpm demonstration passed only because it stopped at
  two objects.
- swtpm runs as unconfined_service_t through a bin_t wrapper. Fedora's
  swtpm-selinux confines it only for libvirt, and every direct route from
  systemd is closed: no transition from init_t (which may not even execute it),
  no init_t -> swtpm_t transition, and no entrypoint for unconfined_service_t.
  Measured against the loaded policy on Fedora 43 and 44.
- State and socket live under swtpm-waydroid, not waydroid-swtpm: Fedora's
  waydroid policy labels /var/lib/waydroid(.*)? and /run/waydroid-(?!lxc).* by
  prefix, and the TPM's seeds should not carry Waydroid's types.
- Drops swtpm's "Data client disconnected" line with LogFilterPatterns=, since
  tcti-swtpm reconnects per TPM command and three checks logged 543 of them;
  swtpm's own --log level does not filter it.
